## 5. Route Map (App Router)

```
app/
  layout.tsx                    # Clerk + Convex providers, fonts, toaster
  globals.css
  page.tsx                      # → redirect to /sign-in if signed out, else /welcome or last app
  sign-in/[[...sign-in]]/page.tsx
  sign-up/[[...sign-up]]/page.tsx
  welcome/page.tsx              # Create new app vs Import from GitHub (coming soon)
  new/
    page.tsx                    # 3-step setup flow (client component w/ state machine)
  app/[appId]/
    layout.tsx                  # Top-right app switcher / new app / profile;
                                # Left collapsible AI panel; bottom: outlet
    page.tsx                    # → redirect to /app/[appId]/prd
    prd/page.tsx
    stack/page.tsx
    knowledge/page.tsx          # grid
    knowledge/[docId]/page.tsx  # editor + back button
    features/page.tsx           # ?view=release|progress (default release)
  api/
    claude/extract-stack/route.ts
    claude/generate-knowledge/route.ts
    claude/extract-features/route.ts
    claude/chat/route.ts        # streaming
    firecrawl/scrape/route.ts
  middleware.ts                 # Clerk auth middleware
```

> Server-side AI/Firecrawl calls may live in Convex actions instead of Next route handlers — final decision in Phase 5. Convex actions are cleaner (auth + DB access in one place); Next routes are easier for streaming responses. Plan: **streaming chat via Next route**, **non-streaming generation via Convex actions**.

